# ODE TO JOY - Beethoven, the finale of the Ninth Symphony, Op. 125 (1824).
# The format is in Demo1/CLAUDE.md, under "Song files". Instruments are tables with
# one entry per frame; each channel holds named tracks; the lines at the end are the
# order list. In a track '.' holds and '-' releases. '#' starts a comment.
#
# Public domain: Beethoven died in 1827. The sixteen-bar tune - F# F# G A A G F# E - written
# from the melody everyone knows, for a level cleared, a victory, a title screen. It plays
# through once in the tune's own simple harmony and loops.
#
# A row is a sixteenth, a line a bar of 4/4 at 128 quarter notes a minute.
#
# What four channels keep. Channel 1 is a short chord on beats two and four; channel 2 the
# tune, in D major and in the octave from A3 to A4, where the pure-tone table is within ten
# cents of every note; channels 3 and 4 a 16-bit bass on beats one and three. The tune's
# repeated notes - F# F#, D D - are each struck again: its instrument starts soft and swells,
# so a note following itself is heard to start.

song   ODE TO JOY
key    D MAJOR

instrument STAB
  table      tone
  volume     10 9 7 5 3 2 1 0
  distortion tone
  release    2

# Brass: in from soft, so a repeated note is heard as struck again.
instrument BRASS
  table      tone
  volume     8 12 13 13 12 12 11 11 11 10
  distortion tone
  release    2

instrument BASS
  table      wide
  volume     12 11 10 9 8 7 6 5 4
  distortion tone
  release    2

channel 1 notes CHORDS
  note  The chord on beats two and four: D, and A for the dominant.
  voice STAB
  track DD . . . .  D . . .  . . . .  D . . .
  track DA . . . .  D . . .  . . . .  A . . .
  track AA . . . .  A . . .  . . . .  A . . .
  track AD . . . .  A . . .  . . . .  D . . .

channel 2 notes TUNE
  note  F# F# G A, A G F# E, D D E F#, F# E E - and the middle, E E F# D.
  voice BRASS
  track O1  F#4 . . .  F#4 . . .  G4 . . .  A4 . . .
  track O2  A4 . . .  G4 . . .  F#4 . . .  E4 . . .
  track O3  D4 . . .  D4 . . .  E4 . . .  F#4 . . .
  track O4  F#4 . . .  . . E4 .  E4 . . .  . . . .
  track O8  E4 . . .  . . D4 .  D4 . . .  . . . .
  track O9  E4 . . .  E4 . . .  F#4 . . .  D4 . . .
  track O10 E4 . . .  F#4 . G4 .  F#4 . . .  D4 . . .
  track O11 E4 . . .  F#4 . G4 .  F#4 . . .  E4 . . .
  track O12 D4 . . .  E4 . . .  A3 . . .  . . . .

channel 3 pair LOW BYTE
  note  The low byte of the bass. AUDCTL 28 joins channels 3 and 4 on the 1.79 MHz clock.

channel 4 notes BASS
  note  Root and fifth on beats one and three.
  voice BASS
  track BD  D2 . . .  . . . .  A1 . . .  . . . .
  track BA  A1 . . .  . . . .  E2 . . .  . . . .
  track BAD A1 . . .  . . . .  D2 . . .  . . . .

# The order list: a line is a bar. Chords, tune, low byte, bass.
speed  7
audctl $28
loop
section ODE
line   DD      O1      .       BD
line   DA      O2      .       BD
line   DD      O3      .       BD
line   AA      O4      .       BA
line   DD      O1      .       BD
line   DA      O2      .       BD
line   DD      O3      .       BD
line   AD      O8      .       BAD
line   AD      O9      .       BAD
line   AD      O10     .       BAD
line   AA      O11     .       BA
line   DA      O12     .       BD
line   DD      O1      .       BD
line   DA      O2      .       BD
line   DD      O3      .       BD
line   AD      O8      .       BAD
